HST Office: HST Sheets dynamic arrays like the leading spreadsheet application, the engine (owner 18/11:
mandatory in 1.0.3). HST-owned code, written clean-room from a behaviour spec, public file-format
specifications and the interface headers of hst-sheets-dynamic-array-hooks.patch, which calls it.

- formula/source/core/hst/hstformulastrings.cxx: formula text. UI grammars (Calc A1, Excel A1) show
  ANCHORARRAY(A1) as A1# and a parenthesised single operand of @ read from a file as @A1:A9; OOXML writes
  @X as _xlfn.SINGLE(X), the operand ending before a separator, an enclosing closing parenthesis, % or a
  binary operator other than the reference operators.
- sc/source/core/hst/hstspillrange.cxx: parsing A1# after a single cell reference ('#' not followed by a
  letter, digit, '#' or non-ASCII character, so #REF!, #N/A stay error constants), also when the '#'
  was scanned inside the symbol (quoted or non-ASCII sheet names); the autocorrected formula keeps A1#.
- sc/source/core/hst/hstdynamicarrayinterpreter.cxx: @ intersects a range with the formula cell's row
  and/or column (#VALUE! when none), takes the upper-left element of an array and leaves single
  values; A1# is the current result size of a dynamic array's anchor as a reference, also one
  cell; #REF! for an empty cell, a constant, an ordinary formula, a legacy array formula, an error
  result or #SPILL!.
- sc/source/ui/hst/hstdynamicarrayinput.cxx: whether a typed formula spills (a formula whose
  outermost function is an array function is a dynamic array whatever its result size; others are
  compiled afresh from the text and calculated once as a Ctrl+Shift+Enter array formula would be,
  unless they can only give one value or call macros, add-ins, DDE or web services);
  the cursor cell alone as entry range when another array is in the way (#SPILL!); the input line
  of a dynamic array without braces.

License: LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary (new files only; the makefile lines are hooks).
Test: CppunitTest_sc_hst_dynamic_arrays (spill, single result, resize, #SPILL! and recovery, blocked by
an array, A1#, A1# of a one-cell result, @, xlsx export/import of Excel's form with cm and round trip,
Spill.xlsx, error constants, text forms in Calc A1 / Excel A1 / OOXML / ODFF).
